    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n282" root="اجر" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِجِّيرَى</span></b>  (ISk, K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِجْرِيَّا</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِجْرِيَّآءُ</span></b>  (S in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هجر</span>) <i>A custom; a habit.</i> (ISk, K, and S
ubi suprà.) The hemzeh is said to be a substitute
for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ه</span> [in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هِجِّيرَى</span> &amp;c.] (TA.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَا زَالَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ذٰلِكَ إِجِّيرَاهُ</span> <i>That ceased not to be his custom,</i> or
<i>habit.</i> (ISk.)

